## Original Content
El Consistorio asegura que durante el Gran Premio no habrá tanta contaminación acústica porque los coches de Fórmula 1 son menos ruidosos.

## Summary
Tests in Madrid have sparked noise complaints, but the City Council states they are indispensable for the Grand Prix. Additionally, it is noted that Formula 1 cars are less noisy, which will reduce noise pollution during the event.

## Key Points
- Noise complaints are arising from tests conducted in Madrid.
- The City Council defends the tests as essential ('imprescindibles').
- Formula 1 cars have reduced noise levels compared to previous models.
- During the Grand Prix, noise pollution is expected to be lower due to these advancements.


